course: dictionary
lesson: 14552
title: A word inside a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and knowing one part can help you with many words. «Phage» is short for bacteriophage. Bacteria are tiny living things, and a phage is a tiny virus that attacks and kills them.
explain: The ending «-phage» comes from Greek and means eat. A macrophage is a big eater: it is a white blood cell that eats germs. «The macrophage ate the germs in my cut.» Once you know the ending, you can guess what a word like this means.
explain: Scientists are now testing phages as medicine. «Doctors are testing phages to fight bacteria that antibiotics cannot kill.» Phages look like tiny space landers, but they are far too small to see without a microscope. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A phage is a tiny virus that attacks and kills bacteria.
fact: Phages do not attack people; they only attack bacteria.
fact: The ending «-phage» comes from Greek and means eat.
fact: A macrophage is a white blood cell that eats germs.
fact: Doctors are testing phage therapy against bacteria that antibiotics cannot kill.
exercise: «Phages are tiny viruses that kill bacteria.» What is a phage? | A large animal that eats plants | *A tiny virus that attacks bacteria | A tool for cutting paper | A kind of sweet, sticky food
exercise: The ending «-phage» means eat. In «macrophage», what does -phage tell you? | Builder | Runner | *Eater | Sleeper
exercise: «Doctors are testing phages against bacteria that antibiotics cannot kill.» Why are doctors interested in phages? | Phages are a kind of vitamin | *Phages might kill bacteria that antibiotics cannot | Phages are used to make bread rise | Phages make people sleepy
test: Does a phage attack people? | *No, it attacks bacteria, not people | Yes, it attacks human cells | Yes, it attacks only plants | Sometimes, when people are asleep
test: What does «macrophage» mean? | A tiny virus | A space lander | A kind of antibiotic | *A white blood cell that eats germs
exam: In «The phage injected its genes into the bacterium», what is a phage? | *A tiny virus that attacks bacteria | A large fish that lives in rivers | A white blood cell that eats people | A tablet to take when you have a cold
